# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js 15 App Router project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Lock file (`package-lock.json`) updated with new dependency tree

### 2. Code Configuration
**Modified: `/src/app/layout.tsx`**
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag at the end (after `{children}`)

This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router (v13.5+), which specifies:
- Using the `@vercel/speed-insights/next` import path for Next.js
- Placing the component in the root layout file
- Adding it inside the body element to collect performance metrics

## Implementation Details

The SpeedInsights component was added according to the latest official Vercel documentation fetched from:
https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

The component will automatically:
- Collect Web Vitals and performance metrics from visitors
- Send data to Vercel's Speed Insights dashboard
- Provide insights on real-world performance after deployment

## Testing & Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ All existing tests pass (107 tests, 0 failures)
✅ No linting errors introduced
✅ Package lock file properly updated
✅ Existing code structure and functionality preserved

